I'm not claiming that it's "normal", whatever that
might mean in a game with countless ways to play it,
merely that "playing without dying" very much is a
"built in by design" optional part of NetHack.

I just had a friend stop playing the online Flash
game Bloons, when he found out that there was a
check-box for infinite ammunition on the opening
screen. I saw that the moment I started the game,
and it didn't bother my game play at all, I just
didn't use it. For him, though, the fact that he
had to _make the choice_ not to use this feature
was sufficient to destroy his pleasure in the game.

So, if you have the mentality that makes _having to
make the choice_ not to pudding farm spoil the game
for you, then you'll want that feature out, because
it causes you too much pain to "just say no".

If you have the strength of character to avoid doing
things that offend you without becoming instead
offended that someone else might do them and thereby
gain advantage _for them in their game_, then you'd
probably agitate instead to leave in any feature
that lets people do what's fun _for them_.

I don't do alchemy, I don't poly-pile, I don't kill
shopkeepers except if I anger one by error, I don't
kill priests to get my donation money refunded, all
things that others do and gloat over doing. It
doesn't make me want to remove these features from
the game because they would offend me if _I_ used
them. That's purely _my_ problem, I have no reason
to make it a problem for others.

In the case, it's probably been over a year since I
last pudding farmed, I may or may not ever do it
again, but I can still see that the capability to do
it is a fun part of the game for those with the huge
amounts of patience/"obsessive compulsive disorder"
to have fun doing it, as I did when I was doing it.

So, should I rant and rave to have it taken out of
the game because it's a feature I won't use? I'd
have to hold my manhood pretty cheap to behave like
that. Instead, I defend it for others because I know
how much _my kind of player_ can find pleasure in
pudding farming, from personal experience.

The many game features that others use to accumulate
ridiculous quantities of HP, PW, and AC don't appeal
to me, a big part of the reason I'm unlikely ever to
ascend. So it goes, I don't begrudge their use to
the majority of NetHack players to whom ascension is
the only point of the game. It just doesn't happen
to be, for me, what the game is about _at all_. To
me, it's a game of managing always insufficient
resources into the teeth of ever increasing
adversity, to see how far I can get without
disaster, full stop. Ascension is something that
might be fun to see, once, but never is also soon
enough.

Were I that hot to see the Planes, or the vibrating
square, I have two well known ways to do that
_without_ first developing sufficient skill to do it
"normally": wizard mode and eXplore mode. That "get
there lazily without building the needed skills" is
one more option to which I have no problem "just
saying no".

Quantum valeat.

